WEBVTT

00:00:01.615 --> 00:00:13.493
Yes, I embraced tenderness and devotion
sou itooshisa to kizuna wo daita

00:00:13.627 --> 00:00:19.199
Floating in unending space
hatenaki umi ni ukabu

00:00:19.199 --> 00:00:26.105
On this small planet
chiisa na hoshi de

00:00:26.640 --> 00:00:37.642
When I feel your warmth next to me
anata no nukumori wo soba ni kanjiru toki

00:00:37.851 --> 00:00:43.790
I understand the burden
inochi no omosa to

00:00:43.790 --> 00:00:51.196
And the transience of life
hakanasa wo shiru no

00:00:53.934 --> 00:00:59.005
Nights of sorrowful wandering
mayoinageku yoru mo

00:00:59.005 --> 00:01:05.879
And tearful mornings
namida no asa mo

00:01:05.879 --> 00:01:11.485
I believe in tomorrow
ashita wo shinjiru kara

00:01:11.485 --> 00:01:17.724
So I can make it through
koeteyukeru no

00:01:17.724 --> 00:01:26.189
To the continuation of the dream
yume no tsuzuki he

00:01:32.472 --> 00:01:37.273
1970 GERMANY. LENNEP

00:01:37.477 --> 00:01:42.312
RUGEN MUSEUM

00:01:42.716 --> 00:01:45.051
-What is this?
-Boy, you're dumb.

00:01:45.051 --> 00:01:47.521
This is the machine that
shoots x-rays!

00:01:47.521 --> 00:01:53.949
As you all know, Professor Rugen
discovered x-rays in the year 1896.

00:01:54.060 --> 00:01:56.797
Teacher, the discovery was an
accident, right?

00:01:56.797 --> 00:02:00.901
That's true. But everything is really
the result of a lot of hard work.

00:02:00.901 --> 00:02:04.962
Come on, further in there's a work
desk he actually used at that time.

00:02:05.472 --> 00:02:08.771
-Let's go!
-Hey, wait!

00:02:48.348 --> 00:02:50.750
Teacher! Gherta is...

00:02:50.750 --> 00:02:52.786
What's the matter?
Did something happen?

00:02:52.786 --> 00:02:54.777
Gherta? Gherta!

00:03:12.506 --> 00:03:15.675
RECOLLECTIONS

00:03:15.675 --> 00:03:17.410
RECOLLECTIONS
Silver-white hair,

00:03:17.410 --> 00:03:18.001
Silver-white hair,

00:03:18.411 --> 00:03:22.349
Eyes of the deep, young sea,

00:03:22.349 --> 00:03:28.822
You cross over all distances.
Like the lovers in the constellations,

00:03:28.822 --> 00:03:32.025
For a brief moment in time,

00:03:32.025 --> 00:03:34.050
sadly coming together.

00:03:35.161 --> 00:03:37.959
The shining light of a
fleeting encounter...

00:03:40.400 --> 00:03:44.097
I want to change it into
something eternal.

00:03:46.006 --> 00:03:49.042
Why does the poem that
Conrad Rugen wrote

00:03:49.042 --> 00:03:52.500
make my heart tremble so?

00:04:20.540 --> 00:04:23.843
Demian. There's no doubt about it.

00:04:23.843 --> 00:04:26.546
27 years ago, in Clairmont...

00:04:26.546 --> 00:04:29.082
He's the boy I met then.

00:04:29.082 --> 00:04:31.778
He's hardly aged at all.

00:04:32.285 --> 00:04:34.583
How can that?

00:04:34.821 --> 00:04:37.346
What is this feeling of terror?

00:04:40.360 --> 00:04:42.362
27 years ago,

00:04:42.362 --> 00:04:46.299
I was asked by an organization from
this country to study the Fragment.

00:04:46.299 --> 00:04:49.736
Two years later,
at 25 years old,

00:04:49.736 --> 00:04:52.238
frustrated with research that
seemed to go nowhere,

00:04:52.238 --> 00:04:54.069
I set out for Clairmont.

00:04:54.140 --> 00:04:57.277
Clairmont, the place where the
Fragment had been discovered.

00:04:57.277 --> 00:05:00.280
Of course, the abandoned factory
from 100 years ago mentioned

00:05:00.280 --> 00:05:02.646
in the records was
no longer there.

00:05:05.552 --> 00:05:08.355
I walked aimlessly around
the city,

00:05:08.355 --> 00:05:13.190
and happened to end up
in front of a certain institution.

00:05:13.293 --> 00:05:16.228
Clairmont Sanatorium?

00:05:29.643 --> 00:05:31.907
It's a nice painting, isn't it?

00:05:36.549 --> 00:05:39.152
I like that painting,

00:05:39.152 --> 00:05:42.019
so sometimes I come here.

00:05:58.672 --> 00:06:01.274
I've been doing some investigating.

00:06:01.274 --> 00:06:04.641
You work at a laboratory on the
Eastern Mainland, correct?

00:06:06.413 --> 00:06:08.711
Are you making progress
with your analysis?

00:06:17.357 --> 00:06:20.326
Who... are you?

00:06:22.796 --> 00:06:25.432
It doesn't matter if
you don't remember.

00:06:25.432 --> 00:06:29.425
You see, I'm very interested in
the research you're doing.

00:06:30.670 --> 00:06:35.341
Unfortunately, I'm not a scientist
so I can't explain in detail,

00:06:35.341 --> 00:06:39.243
but, you see, those codes are the
plans for a certain machine.

00:06:39.446 --> 00:06:42.882
Your research subject at the
German university where you studied,

00:06:42.882 --> 00:06:46.519
the multi-dimensional theory,
it's somewhat related to that.

00:06:46.519 --> 00:06:48.510
How do you know that?

00:06:49.389 --> 00:06:52.552
Look, your trembling has
calmed a bit.

00:06:52.759 --> 00:06:56.991
As I thought, it excites the blood
of such a long-time scientist.

00:06:57.464 --> 00:07:00.797
I'm rushing the completion
of that machine.

00:07:01.434 --> 00:07:04.198
Maybe this will be useful.

00:07:07.273 --> 00:07:09.075
I only got this little bit of
information,

00:07:09.075 --> 00:07:12.704
but I ended up traumatizing
you quite a bit.

00:07:16.349 --> 00:07:20.615
I could never forget
that voice.

00:07:21.054 --> 00:07:25.425
After that, I woke up in the hospital,
and was shocked when I saw this memo.

00:07:25.425 --> 00:07:27.861
The answer to deciphering
the Fragment

00:07:27.861 --> 00:07:30.625
was written in what looked
like a trembling code.

00:07:30.730 --> 00:07:35.360
Who had written it?
Why was this given to me?

00:07:36.569 --> 00:07:39.472
No matter how much I think about it,
I can't understand.

00:07:39.472 --> 00:07:43.272
It's the same choking terror
I get in small rooms.

00:07:43.643 --> 00:07:46.305
Terror...

00:07:50.049 --> 00:07:51.718
Professor Gherta!

00:07:51.718 --> 00:07:53.920
Are you still pulling out
the code?

00:07:53.920 --> 00:07:58.091
Yes. But of course, we're not
getting anything different anymore.

00:07:58.091 --> 00:08:02.228
By the way, Professor, apparently
there was an intruder in this facility.

00:08:02.228 --> 00:08:04.364
A detective from the head office.

00:08:04.364 --> 00:08:07.200
Whatever it is he was looking for,
it's already too late.

00:08:07.200 --> 00:08:09.369
This Fragment is useless as well.

00:08:09.369 --> 00:08:13.439
In a few days, the passageway to death
will be presented to the whole world.

00:08:13.439 --> 00:08:16.943
The Kuril Island Ring is going to
be completed soon, isn't it?

00:08:16.943 --> 00:08:19.312
But in the more than 100 years
since the Fragment

00:08:19.312 --> 00:08:21.371
was put inside this x-ray
machine, it's amazing

00:08:21.481 --> 00:08:24.814
that no one has seen the
piece of stone itself.

00:08:25.218 --> 00:08:28.676
It's still a mystery, isn't it?
Where it came from?

00:08:32.292 --> 00:08:36.462
When Kirchner disappeared...
That black mist...

00:08:36.462 --> 00:08:38.731
Stop development immediately!

00:08:38.731 --> 00:08:42.132
The Zone should never
have been meddled with!

00:08:42.735 --> 00:08:44.999
Zone?

00:08:45.438 --> 00:08:50.375
The Children of Befort.
Who in the world are they?

00:09:02.188 --> 00:09:04.418
Wonder!

00:09:05.725 --> 00:09:07.060
Helga!

00:09:07.060 --> 00:09:08.254
Okay!

00:09:12.665 --> 00:09:14.155
Thank you, Thoma.

00:09:16.736 --> 00:09:19.505
This sanatorium is where the person
you were in the life before this one,

00:09:19.505 --> 00:09:24.374
the artist named Serafine, lived until
the day she died after she became ill.

00:09:32.685 --> 00:09:37.816
I... Why... did I do that?

00:09:38.925 --> 00:09:40.460
Thoma!

00:09:40.460 --> 00:09:43.062
What are you doing?!
We're going!

00:09:43.062 --> 00:09:44.825
Okay!

00:09:45.798 --> 00:09:50.895
By the time we managed to get here,
she had already passed away.

00:10:14.060 --> 00:10:16.324
It's the same as Helga's picture!

00:11:18.791 --> 00:11:21.385
Serafine...

00:11:23.329 --> 00:11:24.887
Helga?

00:11:48.554 --> 00:11:50.123
Are you okay?

00:11:50.123 --> 00:11:51.954
Yeah...

00:11:54.060 --> 00:11:57.427
This was Serafine's sickroom.

00:12:01.234 --> 00:12:03.669
Do you remember anything?

00:12:03.669 --> 00:12:05.193
No.

00:12:05.338 --> 00:12:09.775
This was where she breathed
her last. In that bed.

00:12:14.247 --> 00:12:16.215
Helga!

00:12:20.753 --> 00:12:22.622
Are you okay, Helga?

00:12:22.622 --> 00:12:24.457
Aren't you just wrong about this?!

00:12:24.457 --> 00:12:28.795
It's useless! Doing this kind of thing
just makes Helga suffer!

00:12:28.795 --> 00:12:31.195
Helga, let's go!

00:12:33.599 --> 00:12:36.636
Over there... There's something...

00:12:36.636 --> 00:12:40.606
A straight road.
And next to it...

00:12:40.606 --> 00:12:45.737
That's right. The house where
Serafine was born is over there.

00:12:51.117 --> 00:12:53.920
Where is Tina?

00:12:53.920 --> 00:12:56.422
Soon, soon...

00:12:56.422 --> 00:13:00.483
You keep telling me that, but almost
13 years have passed already.

00:13:01.260 --> 00:13:05.031
Here that would be 260 years
that have gone by.

00:13:05.031 --> 00:13:07.522
In that case, why don't you
look for her, Father?

00:13:09.435 --> 00:13:13.339
We know what would happen if
we went outside with our bodies.

00:13:13.339 --> 00:13:15.967
We're not ignorant like you.

00:13:16.008 --> 00:13:17.944
Prince Dumas, it's because
you are young

00:13:17.944 --> 00:13:21.345
that the anatomic atrophy of
this planet is possible.

00:13:22.648 --> 00:13:26.018
My body can no longer
return to normal!

00:13:26.018 --> 00:13:28.754
That's a trivial matter, Dumas.

00:13:28.754 --> 00:13:31.124
I will return to Greecia.

00:13:31.124 --> 00:13:34.760
It's only so I can get revenge by
overthrowing King Titus

00:13:34.760 --> 00:13:37.456
that I keep on living like this.

00:13:37.563 --> 00:13:40.566
Greecia is mine, Dumas.

00:13:40.566 --> 00:13:43.169
We only need Tina!

00:13:43.169 --> 00:13:45.831
There's no need to stay
on this planet so long.

00:14:18.404 --> 00:14:20.201
Helga...

00:14:55.241 --> 00:14:59.679
Just get out of here!
All you are is a nuisance! Go on!

00:14:59.679 --> 00:15:02.515
Oh, Serafine! Taking a walk?

00:15:02.515 --> 00:15:04.283
Jim! You're here!

00:15:04.283 --> 00:15:07.820
Miss Serafine.
Isn't there any way?

00:15:07.820 --> 00:15:09.689
Even if it's just one or two pieces.

00:15:09.689 --> 00:15:11.857
She said no, didn't she?!
Go home!

00:15:11.857 --> 00:15:16.462
As if a shady art dealer like you
could appreciate those paintings!

00:15:16.462 --> 00:15:20.933
I'm not talking to you!
Besides, you're not even related to her!

00:15:20.933 --> 00:15:22.602
What did you say?!

00:15:22.602 --> 00:15:25.004
I'm sorry, Mr. Ude.

00:15:25.004 --> 00:15:29.134
I don't paint those pictures
to sell them.

00:15:31.677 --> 00:15:34.271
To me, those pictures are...

00:15:35.681 --> 00:15:39.242
To me, those pictures are...

00:15:39.585 --> 00:15:43.112
They're like a light burning
in the darkness.

00:15:44.790 --> 00:15:46.985
They're very precious.

00:15:47.660 --> 00:15:49.855
That's why I can't give them
to you.

00:15:50.463 --> 00:15:52.624
I see.

00:15:53.899 --> 00:15:56.969
But I'm not going to give up!
I'll come again.

00:15:56.969 --> 00:15:58.869
Never come back!

00:15:59.872 --> 00:16:03.309
Jim was really threatening
the last time he was here as well!

00:16:03.309 --> 00:16:05.743
He rolled over three times
in the garden!

00:16:06.445 --> 00:16:08.948
But I'm glad that Jim was here.

00:16:08.948 --> 00:16:11.150
It's nothing, Serafine.

00:16:11.150 --> 00:16:13.819
I'm the one who comes over
here like it's my own home.

00:16:13.819 --> 00:16:16.287
Your father and mother spoil me.

00:16:16.589 --> 00:16:20.226
Jim, thank you for doing all this
for my parents.

00:16:20.226 --> 00:16:22.595
You can stay a little longer
today, can't you?

00:16:22.595 --> 00:16:24.620
Make yourself at home.

00:16:36.642 --> 00:16:38.244
It's all right, ma'am.

00:16:38.244 --> 00:16:43.282
But it's just that we're worried
about her and you as well, Jim.

00:16:43.282 --> 00:16:46.185
We're getting on in years,

00:16:46.185 --> 00:16:48.287
so as long as it's okay
with you, Jim...

00:16:48.287 --> 00:16:50.556
And we know what your feelings are.

00:16:50.556 --> 00:16:57.257
Sir, ma'am, there's no room for me
in Serafine's heart.

00:16:57.730 --> 00:16:59.332
I understand that.

00:16:59.332 --> 00:17:03.393
But it's okay, I intend to stay
by her side always.

00:17:03.502 --> 00:17:05.671
That's what I want to do.

00:17:05.671 --> 00:17:08.196
If Serafine will allow me to.

00:17:11.010 --> 00:17:13.079
Serafine, I'm going home.

00:17:13.079 --> 00:17:17.149
Thank you, Jim. When will you
be able to come again?

00:17:17.149 --> 00:17:20.710
I'm heading for India,
so it'll be about a month.

00:17:21.220 --> 00:17:23.222
So long?

00:17:23.222 --> 00:17:25.324
A month will go by in no time!

00:17:25.324 --> 00:17:28.851
But you'll probably forget all
about me.

00:17:48.581 --> 00:17:51.049
You're Miss Serafine, right?

00:17:53.419 --> 00:17:57.287
I was told to give this to you.
It's from Jim.

00:18:00.559 --> 00:18:02.288
Where's Jim?

00:18:03.596 --> 00:18:06.258
He passed away.

00:18:19.011 --> 00:18:22.648
That handkerchief belonged to an old
woman who, when we arrived in India,

00:18:22.648 --> 00:18:26.218
happened to be visiting there
from Spain.

00:18:26.218 --> 00:18:29.789
Jim begged her to let him have it.

00:18:29.789 --> 00:18:32.124
It was apparently something
she'd gotten from her teacher,

00:18:32.124 --> 00:18:34.888
and the old woman
was really at a loss.

00:18:35.027 --> 00:18:36.962
But he desperately wanted
to give it to you

00:18:36.962 --> 00:18:39.265
So he could tell you about it.

00:18:39.265 --> 00:18:42.132
He kept it with him and
was very careful with it.

00:18:46.572 --> 00:18:49.302
On our way home the seas
were very rough.

00:18:51.877 --> 00:18:53.179
The handkerchief!

00:18:53.179 --> 00:18:55.170
Stop, Jim!

00:18:58.217 --> 00:19:00.419
Give this to Serafine!

00:19:00.419 --> 00:19:03.786
To Serafine!

00:19:06.392 --> 00:19:10.123
We tried our best to
save him, but...

00:19:12.064 --> 00:19:16.296
For my sake...

00:20:06.685 --> 00:20:09.381
Do you remember me, Miss Serafine?

00:20:09.555 --> 00:20:11.423
I'm Ude.

00:20:11.423 --> 00:20:14.426
Please forgive me for
my rudeness in the past.

00:20:14.426 --> 00:20:16.862
I was just a foolish young man.

00:20:16.862 --> 00:20:19.490
Obsessed with making
a name for myself.

00:20:19.632 --> 00:20:22.032
I see you're still painting.

00:20:23.702 --> 00:20:27.866
Ever since then,
they've always stayed in my heart.

00:20:29.708 --> 00:20:32.905
They truly are mysterious pictures.

00:20:59.004 --> 00:21:02.906
Jim... For my sake...

00:21:03.442 --> 00:21:05.171
Helga!

00:21:07.546 --> 00:21:09.537
Helga...

00:21:29.535 --> 00:21:33.767
A small light burning
in the darkness...

00:21:39.345 --> 00:21:41.472
You've remembered, haven't you?

00:21:49.521 --> 00:21:53.082
Teacher! Miss Christina!

00:21:56.528 --> 00:21:59.565
Christina!

00:21:59.565 --> 00:22:01.999
-Aghi!
-Yes.

00:22:03.702 --> 00:22:05.363
Helga.

00:22:07.306 --> 00:22:10.242
Our eighteenth reincarnation
was right around

00:22:10.242 --> 00:22:12.836
the beginning of the 19th century.

00:22:13.045 --> 00:22:15.775
A student of Christina's had this.

00:22:15.981 --> 00:22:18.814
The handkerchief Jim gave me.

00:22:37.236 --> 00:22:47.043
At the bottom of the deep, clear sea
fukaku fukaku sukitooru umi no soko ni

00:22:47.312 --> 00:22:57.156
A small flower is resting
chiisana hana madoronderu

00:22:57.156 --> 00:23:01.889
The melody of a gentle wind
amayaka na kaze no shirabe

00:23:01.927 --> 00:23:06.762
Passes through a rainbow
niji wo kuguri

00:23:07.166 --> 00:23:16.302
The fish are playing in the sky
sakanatachi wa sora ni asobu

00:23:16.442 --> 00:23:21.480
Everyone plays the music of love
dare mo ga ai wo kanaderu

00:23:21.480 --> 00:23:26.752
A warm light came down
atatakana hikari futteta

00:23:26.752 --> 00:23:31.155
(A gaze) That gaze
(manazashi wa) sono manazashi wa

00:23:31.190 --> 00:23:35.494
Is unbound and becomes full
hodokete michiteku

00:23:35.494 --> 00:23:40.363
Embraced by water
mizu ni dakare
